  "Id": 927,
  "Title": "Chief Minister Sindh visits AKUH to see bomb blast patients",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Sindh Chief Minister Sardar Ali Mohammad Mahar visited Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH) on May 27, 2004 to inquire about the progress of the victims of the May 26 bomb blasts on Fatima Jinnah Road in Karachi .",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassCAF2318E142F42898C06FB4E5C372528\"><div>Sindh Chief Minister Sardar Ali Mohammad Mahar visited Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH) on May 27, 2004 to inquire about the progress of the victims of the May 26 bomb blasts on Fatima Jinnah Road in Karachi.</div><div><br></div><div>Eleven injured, including nine policemen and two civilians, were brought to AKUH in the aftermath of the blasts. Currently, five patients are still under treatment at the Hospital. AKUH's multidisciplinary approach to diagnosis and care ensures a continuum of safe and high-quality care for patients.</div><div><br></div><div>The Chief Minister expressed satisfaction with the compassionate and high-quality care being provided to the patients currently under treatment at AKUH. He praised the administration, doctors and staff of AKUH for their timely and professional response to this crisis.</div></div>",
